cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use QuGrid in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "QuGrid: quantum computing for power system research"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Cao
    given-names: Travis
repository-code: "https://github.com/TravisCao/qugrid"
url: "https://traviscao.github.io/qugrid/"
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-08-13"
keywords:
  - power systems
  - quantum computing
  - QUBO
  - QAOA
  - HHL
  - unit commitment
  - power flow
abstract: >-
  QuGrid is a research library that connects power system data and problems
  (MATPOWER/pandapower networks, unit commitment, islanding, PMU placement,
  power flow, security screening) to quantum algorithms (QAOA, VQE, HHL, VQLS,
  quantum kernels, quantum Boltzmann machines) through exact, tested
  encodings, with classical baselines and honest benchmarking built into
  every result.
